&lt;p class=&quot;PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer&quot; data-start=&quot;135&quot; data-end=&quot;148&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;150&quot; data-end=&quot;218&quot;&gt;Own the firmware that brings Graphcore hardware and silicon to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;220&quot; data-end=&quot;431&quot;&gt;As a Staff Firmware Engineer, you will design, develop and deliver firmware for Graphcore’s next generation products. Your work will sit close to the hardware and shape how our systems boot, run and communicate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;433&quot; data-end=&quot;633&quot;&gt;You will help build the software that supports complete hardware bootup, silicon interaction, telemetry and monitoring. Your code will connect silicon, drivers, host systems and datacentre operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;635&quot; data-end=&quot;831&quot;&gt;You will take part in technical design discussions across Graphcore and with partners. You will also help engineers solve complex firmware problems and raise engineering standards across the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;833&quot; data-end=&quot;961&quot;&gt;This role suits someone who wants deep technical ownership, real system complexity and the chance to influence product delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;963&quot; data-end=&quot;983&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team and Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;985&quot; data-end=&quot;1164&quot;&gt;The Firmware team writes the software that enables Graphcore hardware and silicon to start, operate and report reliably. The work is practical, technical and close to the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1166&quot; data-end=&quot;1341&quot;&gt;Engineers are expected to own outcomes, speak up in design discussions and move work forward. Decisions are shaped through technical debate, code reviews and Agile ceremonies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1343&quot; data-end=&quot;1529&quot;&gt;You will work with firmware specialists, system software engineers, partners and wider product teams. The pace is focused, with responsibility shared by people who understand the detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1531&quot; data-end=&quot;1553&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1555&quot; data-end=&quot;2056&quot;&gt;· Strong embedded software engineering experience using C or C++&lt;br&gt;· Experience designing and implementing real-time embedded systems using Zephyr or a similar RTOS&lt;br&gt;· Proven ability to understand, build and debug complex embedded platforms&lt;br&gt;· Clear problem-solving skills and the ability to drive outcomes independently&lt;br&gt;· Strong communication skills, including documenting complex system designs clearly&lt;br&gt;· Solid understanding of Continuous Integration, build systems and software packaging best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2058&quot; data-end=&quot;2270&quot;&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. We also welcome engineers returning to the profession after a career break, including through returnship routes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2272&quot; data-end=&quot;2280&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2282&quot; data-end=&quot;3180&quot;&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work Comment by Helen Doyle: can we take out unlimited as its not contractual and change to generous or flexible.&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3182&quot; data-end=&quot;3544&quot;&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3546&quot; data-end=&quot;3557&quot;&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3559&quot; data-end=&quot;3715&quot;&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3717&quot; data-end=&quot;3743&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;3745&quot; data-end=&quot;4024&quot;&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4026&quot; data-end=&quot;4308&quot;&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4310&quot; data-end=&quot;4632&quot;&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;4634&quot; data-end=&quot;4776&quot; data-is-last-node=&quot;&quot; data-is-only-node=&quot;&quot;&gt;If you want to shape the firmware behind Graphcore’s next generation systems, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to be part of the journey.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Backend Engineer on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/ai/agent-foundations/agent-developer/&quot;&gt;Flow Components functional team&lt;/a&gt;, you&#39;ll help build GitLab&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/modelops/applied-ml/code-suggestions/ai-assist/-/tree/main/docs/flow_registry?ref_type=heads&quot;&gt;Flow Registry,&lt;/a&gt; which provides reusable primitives for agentic flows built on the GitLab Duo Agent Platform. Your primary focus will be backend engineering in Python, using LangChain and LangGraph to develop secure, reliable, and scalable capabilities across the Duo Workflow Service and the GitLab monolith. You&#39;ll also work across the stack when needed, bringing familiarity with JavaScript and frontend development to support the official GitLab Duo Agent Platform client, Duo CLI, and advocate for a strong user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Develop, ship, and maintain secure, well-tested, and performant Flow Registry features across the Duo Workflow Service and the GitLab monolith backend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Product Management, User Experience, frontend, backend, and artificial intelligence specialists to refine requirements and deliver iterative product improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Design, implement, and review GraphQL and REST application programming interfaces, related backend logic, and clear contracts with frontend clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Improve automated testing with RSpec and other frameworks to strengthen quality, reliability, and developer feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Share standards, patterns, and lessons with other engineers to support responsible artificial intelligence integration and evidence-driven engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Participate in Tier 2 on-call rotations, troubleshoot production issues, contribute to root cause analysis, and improve observability and resiliency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Monitor the competitive landscape and help keep GitLab&#39;s Flow Registry primitives and capabilities competitive within the agentic platform market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Experience building and maintaining production Python applications with LangChain and LangGraph, including background jobs, application programming interfaces, and data models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Experience designing and shipping artificial intelligence-powered backend features and integrations, with sound judgment about large language model limitations and responsible production use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Proficiency in designing or extending REST and GraphQL application programming interfaces with attention to scalability, maintainability, and backward compatibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Strong SQL skills and familiarity with relational databases such as PostgreSQL, including efficient queries and data modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Comfort working across the stack in a mature codebase and addressing performance bottlenecks at the application and, when relevant, infrastructure layers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Familiarity with JavaScript and Vue frontend development, with an understanding of user experience principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including experience writing technical proposals and documentation and collaborating in a remote, asynchronous, cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Openness to learning and applying transferable skills from related technologies or domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work across backend, frontend, User Experience, Product Management, and artificial intelligence disciplines to improve capabilities such as Memory and Duo Developer and support clients including Duo CLI. We collaborate in GitLab&#39;s remote, asynchronous environment to build reliable components that help people create and use agentic workflows.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re in an unbelievably exciting area of tech and are fundamentally reshaping the data storage industry. Here, you lead with innovative thinking, grow along with us, and join the smartest team in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This type of work—work that changes the world—is what the tech industry was founded on. So, if you&#39;re ready to seize the endless opportunities and leave your mark, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Lead&amp;nbsp; Product Services Engineer role is critical to building the foundation of scalable services at Everpure. You will define how Product capabilities are operationalised, ensuring that product adoption is supported by consistent, high-quality service frameworks. The role is responsible for engineering and operationalising repeatable platform services that support the lifecycle of Everpure products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Role is expected to demonstrate the appropriate level of technical and thought leadership and internal cross-functional influence, as well as to devise new quality methods, content and innovations to accelerate enablement and influence quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leading another Platform Services Engineer, the role is responsible for driving and ensuring completion of all delivery readiness requirements, as well as the automation, and standardisation of product-attached services, ensuring they can be deployed consistently, efficiently, and at global scale. Working closely with Product Engineering, Portfolio, and Delivery teams, the role translates product capabilities into scalable service offerings that improve operational efficiency and accelerate customer adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define Platform services scope&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define a robust Delivery Readiness Framework for successful deployment (integrating with existing workflows)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define service readiness criteria, operational documentation, and enablement assets before global release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define &amp;amp; Establish service standards, quality measures, SLAs, and operational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure product services are aligned to product releases and engineering roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery Operational Readiness:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the intersection between Product Engineering &amp;amp; Advanced Services ensuring every product service is operationally ready prior to release (Field Testing / QA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Engineering to operationalise new platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Engineering / Product Team on Tech Documentation ( version control / management)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify Enablement requirements (Partners, CDP, ASP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing Software Release impact assessment and notifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Services Engineering Lab Management strategy / Overview&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation (Continuous Improvement &amp;amp; Automation)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adopt a Six Sigma type approach to continuous improvement / efficiencies in workflows and technology through automation, simplification, and standardisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with an AI innovation mindset - Develop service automation, tooling, runbooks, and operational procedures to improve consistency and quality and&amp;nbsp; constantly enhance scalable service frameworks that improve operational efficiency &amp;amp; accelerate customer adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Platform Services Engineer(s)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Program Management approach /&amp;nbsp; governance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close collaboration with Stakeholders / Leadership Teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Technical SME for wider Implementation Center of Excellence Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in Product engineering, infrastructure, or cloud environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of product lifecycle and operational service design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building automation and standardised operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise Products (storage, cloud, virtualization, networking)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting or automation tools (e.g. Terraform, Python, CI/CD pipelines)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design scalable, repeatable service models rather than one-off solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills across architecture, product, and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail and focus on operational excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Documentation and asset management (version control) skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge / experience&amp;nbsp; of Continuous Improvement Methodologies (ie Six Sigma) preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU CAN EXPECT FROM US:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;: We celebrate those who think critically, like a challenge, and aspire to be trailblazers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth&lt;/strong&gt;: We give you the space and support to grow along with us and to contribute to something meaningful. We have been named Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in Technology™, Fortune&#39;s Best Workplaces in the Bay Area™, and certified as a Great Place to Work®!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team&lt;/strong&gt;: We build each other up and set aside ego for the greater good.&lt;/li&gt;
